                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "can you explain a litte bit more on how applications like pldm could use this feature, and what is the guarantee that the recover works e.t.c, and in that case show should applications react ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi, I have some comments."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 552,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Why don't you wrap the whole `recoverMctpEndpoint` into #ifdef MCTP_RECOVERY? Because it won't be used in the opposite condition anyway."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 552,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I am considering that if we wrap the whole recoverMctpEndpoint into #ifdef MCTP_RECOVERY, in the future, if new code calls recoverMctpEndpoint without the corresponding #ifdef, the code with MCTP_RECOVERY enabled by default will build successfully, but the code with MCTP_RECOVERY disabled by default will cause a compilation failure."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 552,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Oh that makes sense. So do you think we should place [maybe_unused] right in the argument position of the function, thenn uder #else, we can log some info?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I think it should be `allow-mctp-endpoint-recovery`. And the description should be clearer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I can modify this, but do you suggest adding more details to the description to explain the motivation? Or do you have any suggestions on how to modify it?\nThank you very much."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, I personally see it does not dictate enough what this config does. I expect it to at least quote some words from the commit that handles this call. Something like:\n\n> Support handling the timeout error code returned from a communication to an endpoint by calling to the `.Recover` method under `au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP.Endpoint1` published by mctpd. This requests a check to the endpoint's availability and handles accordingly by continuing to communicate or removing the endpoint depending on the next behaviors of mctpd.\n\nYou can use your own words, but it should explain more than the current ones."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you guys think why can someone specifically disable this feature ? I would expect that people would want this by default, right ? Trying to understand if this really needs to be a configurable option - if people are never going to disable it then , its not worth to give that flexibility to the user right ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "This is because the current `MCTP recovery` method is designed for `dynamic EID`, but in systems that already use a `static EID` architecture and are prone to `PLDM request timeouts`, calling the `MCTP recovery` method can cause unexpected changes to the EID, which in turn affects the system."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "then please start a discussion on codeconstruct/mctp to prevent recovery for static EIDs. I don't think this should be a build-time option on mctpd"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the suggestion.\nWe\u2019ll focus on addressing the recovery method for static EIDs rather than making it a build-time option in mctpd."
                }
            ],
